      "problem": "Evaluate ${}_{8}{C}_{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ and $r=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{8}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{8!}{(8-3)!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{5!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{5!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6}{6} \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
